# Architecture

## Server state vs client state

- **TanStack Query:** meals, profile, nutrition, recipes, recommendations, statistics, any API/DB data
- **Pinia:** modals, tabs, sidebar, seasonal theme, form input values before submit

Query never stores UI state. Pinia never caches API responses.

## Folders

```
src/assets              # static files; SVG under icons/, auth/, landing/, …
src/components/{common,dashboard,meals,recommendations,auth,profile}
src/views
src/composables
src/queries
src/stores
src/services          # supabase/, openFoodFacts, theMealDb — NOT Gemini
                      # supabase/: client, connection, errors, stub (frontend DB/Auth access)
src/router
src/locales/{uk,en}   # common, auth, dashboard, meals (no hardcoded copy)
src/styles/base.css
src/styles/themes     # autumn, winter, spring, summer
src/styles/views      # one CSS file per route name (landing.css, login.css, …)
src/styles/components # one CSS file per component (app-button.css, …)
src/types
src/constants         # domain constants — no magic values in components
src/utils
supabase/functions/{analyze-photo,analyze-text}
```

Views (routes): Landing, Login, Register, Onboarding, Dashboard, AddMeal, MyMeals, Recommendations, Profile. AI Estimator is a separate view or part of AddMeal (post-MVP).

View styles: `src/styles/views/{ROUTE_NAMES value}.css`. Component styles: `src/styles/components/{kebab-component-name}.css`. Import from the Vue `<script setup>` — no `<style>` blocks in SFCs.

## Flows

- User data: Vue → Supabase (RLS)
- Product search: Vue → Open Food Facts (service + query); fallback — manual macros
- Recipes: Vue → TheMealDB; fallback — Recommendations unavailable, rest of the app works
- AI: Vue → Edge Function → Gemini → calorie estimate only. Key never in the client

## Data model

User, UserProfile, Food, Meal, MealIngredient, DailyEntry, AIRequest.
Do not keep AI photos longer than needed for processing.
